# Every change needs a look from the maintainer. On a single-maintainer
# fork this doesn't gate a second pair of eyes the way it would on a team
# repo — the value here is narrower: it's what makes GitHub's "require
# review from Code Owners" branch-protection rule enforceable at all, and
# it stops Renovate (or anyone with write access later) from merging
# something on this repo's behalf without a human in the loop.

